title: Absolute page names are silently wiki-relative — decide and pin
updated: 2026-11-03T04:43:18Z
---

Found in the 0.002 release check (E2E run against the image raudssus/mcp-wiki:0.002).

`rename_page from=Projekt.md to=/tmp/weg.md` succeeds and moves the page to `<wiki>/tmp/weg.md` (commit "Renamed page: Projekt.md -> tmp/weg.md"). Confinement holds — nothing is written outside the root — because `_walk_page` splits on `/+` and skips empty parts, so a leading slash is a no-op (lib/MCP/Wiki/Server.pm, `_walk_page`).

Not a security defect, but undecided and unpinned:
- t/36-server-path-security.t has no case with an absolute name (`/etc/passwd`, `/tmp/x.md`).
- The tool descriptions say "relative to the wiki root" but not what happens with an absolute one.
- A client that means a real absolute path gets a surprise file inside the wiki.

Decide: refuse absolute names ("Path outside wiki root") or accept them as wiki-relative on purpose. Either way pin it in t/36 for every tool and say it in the page parameter description. Not a release blocker.
